      "text": "To convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to Chinese yuan, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert Namibian dollars to US dollars:**\n   - Given: 1 US dollar = 7 Namibian dollars\n   - We need to find out how many US dollars are equivalent to 105 Namibian dollars.\n\n   Let's set up the ratio:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\text{US dollars}}{\\text{Namibian dollars}} = \\frac{1}{7}\n   \\]\n\n   Cross-multiplying gives:\n   \\[\n   \\text{US dollars} \\times 7 = \\text{Namibian dollars}\n   \\]\n   Solving for US dollars:\n   \\[\n   \\text{US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Namibian dollars}}{7}\n   \\]\n\n   Substituting the value of 105 Namibian dollars into the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\text{US dollars} = \\frac{105}{7} = 15\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert US dollars to Chinese yuan:**\n   - Given: 1 US dollar = 6 Chinese yuan\n   - We now need to find out how many Chinese yuan are equivalent to 15 US dollars.\n\n   Using the same ratio:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\text{Chinese yuan}}{\\text{US dollars}} = \\frac{1}{6}\n   \\]\n\n   Cross-multiplying gives:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Chinese yuan} \\times 6 = \\text{US dollars}\n   \\]\n   Solving for Chinese yuan:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Chinese yuan} = \\frac{\\text{US dollars}}{6}\n   \\]\n\n   Substituting the value of 15 US dollars into the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Chinese yuan} = \\frac{15}{6} = 2.5\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of 105 Namibian dollars in Chinese yuan is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2.5}\n\\]",
